{"text": "Polaroid's Newest--'The Swinger'\nBoston Globe (1960-1979); Jul 14, 1965;\n\npg. 18\n\nA less-than-\u00a720 Polaroid\n\u2018Land camera that\u2019 literally\ngays \u201cyes\u201d in the viewfinder\nwhen the exposure setting is\nerfect to take .a 10-second\nJack-and-white picture, was\nannounced by Polaroid Cor-\nporation Tuesday.\nThe new Model 20 Land\nCamera, to be called \u201cThe\nSwinger,\" marks Polaroid's\n\u2018entry in to the mass market\nswith a camera priced in the\n\u2018ange which represents 70\nercent of the nation\u2019s cam~-\nera volume.\n* First sales of The Swinger ;\nwill be in retail stores in Can-\n\u2018ada starting July 24. The on-\n\u2018sale date in the United States\nhas not been set firmly yet,\nbut according to Polaroid na-\n\ntional sales manager Tom\nPeirce, it might be mid-Sep-\ntember. \u201cIntroduction of the\nnew camera in the U.S.A,\u201d he\nsaid, \u201cwould be determined\nprimarily by the date Pola-\nroid catches up with the \u2018runa-\nway success\u2019 of the two new-\nest Polaroid color pack cam-\neras that were introduced last\nSpring.\n\u201cDespite the fact that we\nhave doubled production of\nour color pack camera since\n\nPolaroid\u2019s Newest\u2014\u2018The Swinger\u2019\n\nApril 1, we still have not \u00a2\ncaught up with the demand |\nand it appears now it will be \u2018\nlate August or early Septem-\nber before our production can\nmeet the demand. .\n\u201cTo introduce The Swinger\nat this time,\u201d he said, \u201cwould\nadd confusion to our distribu-\ntion and wo have elected to\nwait so we can launch this\nnew inexpensive camera in\nthe U.S.A, in a more orderly\nfashion,\n\nReproduced with permission of the copyright owner. Further reproduction prohibited without permission.",
